{# Bin days. The load-bearing fact: the three-week grey/blue/purple rotation
   runs in the same phase across all of Largs — verified against the council's
   own calendars 3A and 3B for a full year, in which the coloured weeks never
   once differ. So the colour needs no postcode and no lookup. Only the weekday
   varies by street, and the brown bin alternates between the two calendars;
   both of those questions go to the council's own checker. Nothing here is
   fetched — it is computed from a verified anchor week in src/_data/bins.cjs. #}

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="thisweek-h">
  <h2 id="thisweek-h" class="visually-hidden">This week</h2>

  {% import "tile-icons.njk" as icons %}
  {% if bins.current.note %}
  <p class="sample-note">{{ bins.current.note }}</p>
  {% else %}
  <div class="bin-now">
    {{ icons.bin(bins.current.swatch, "bin-glyph bin-glyph-lg") }}
    <div>
      <div class="bin-now-label">This week in Largs</div>
      <div class="bin-now-colour">{{ bins.current.name }} bin</div>
      <div class="bin-now-sub">{{ bins.current.holds }} · week beginning Monday {{ bins.current.startLong }}</div>
      <div class="bin-now-brown">Brown bin this week for
      {{ bins.current.brownCalendar }} streets — {{ bins.current.brownCalendarNext }}
      streets have it next week.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="note">Your collection day depends on your street — somewhere between
  Monday and Friday. The colour does not: every household in Largs puts out the
  same coloured bin in the same week.</p>

  <h3 class="bin-ahead-head">The next three weeks</h3>
  <ul class="bin-ahead">
    {% for w in bins.ahead %}
    <li>
      {{ icons.bin(w.swatch, "bin-glyph bin-glyph-sm") }}
      <span class="bin-ahead-colour">{{ w.name }}</span>
      <span class="bin-ahead-when">week of {{ w.startShort }}</span>
      <span class="bin-ahead-brown">brown: {{ w.brownCalendar }} streets</span>
      {% if w.note %}<span class="bin-ahead-note">{{ w.note }}</span>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="brown-h">
  <h2 id="brown-h">The brown bin, and which calendar you are on</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <p class="page-intro">Largs is covered by two of the council's collection
  calendars, <strong>3A</strong> and <strong>3B</strong>. For the grey, blue and
  purple bins the two are identical — the same colour in the same week, every
  week of the year. The only difference between them is the brown bin, which is
  fortnightly and falls a week apart: when 3A puts brown out, 3B does not, and
  the week after they swap.</p>

  <p class="note">So there is one thing worth checking once. Look your address up
  on the council's checker, see which week your brown bin falls in, and match it
  against the panel above — that tells you whether you are 3A or 3B, and it stays
  the same from then on. Brown often lands on a different day from your coloured
  bin: a Monday street might have brown on the Wednesday, a Friday street on the
  Tuesday.</p>

  <p class="note">Brown also stops entirely over the festive fortnight, in
  different weeks for each calendar, while the coloured bins keep running. The
  council announce those dates each December.</p>

  <a class="more" href="{{ bins.checkerUrl }}">Check your address on the council's checker →</a>
</section>

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="which-h">
  <h2 id="which-h">Which bin takes what</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <ul class="bin-key">
    {% for c in bins.order %}
    <li>
      {{ icons.bin(c.swatch, "bin-glyph bin-glyph-sm") }}
      <span class="bin-key-name">{{ c.name }}</span>
      <span class="bin-key-holds">{{ c.holds }}</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
    <li>
      {{ icons.bin(bins.brown.swatch, "bin-glyph bin-glyph-sm") }}
      <span class="bin-key-name">{{ bins.brown.name }}</span>
      <span class="bin-key-holds">{{ bins.brown.holds }} · fortnightly, separate round</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="note">Bins should be out at the kerbside by 7am on your collection
  day. The council's pages have the detail on what belongs in each bin, missed
  collections, caddies and bulky uplifts.</p>

  <a class="more" href="{{ bins.councilUrl }}">Bins, litter and recycling at North Ayrshire Council →</a>
</section>

<section class="wrap council-page council-last" aria-labelledby="how-h">
  <h2 id="how-h">How this page works</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <p class="note">The rotation was checked against eight addresses across Largs,
  one on every collection weekday from Routenburn Road to Bowen Craig, and then
  against a full year of the council's own printed calendars 3A and 3B. Their
  coloured weeks are identical throughout — no week of the year carries two
  coloured bins, and the sequence runs unbroken through the festive weeks, when
  only the days move. This page counts the weeks forward from that verified
  point. It is not a live feed from the council, so around Christmas and New
  Year treat the council's own page as the answer. Last checked
  {{ bins.verified | dateLong }}.</p>
</section>
